        <div class="content-text">
          <p>SE tax rate. For <span data-field="year">{{ year }}</span>, the Old Age, Survivors, and Disability Insurance (OASDI) portion of the SE tax remains at <span data-field="rate_oasdi">{{ rate_oasdi }}</span>. The Medicare (HI) portion of the SE tax remains at <span data-field="rate_hi">{{ rate_hi }}</span>. As a result, the SE tax rate remains at <span data-field="total_rate">{{ total_rate }}</span>. For more information, see the Instructions for Schedule SE (Form 1040).</p>
          <p>Earnings subject to social security. For <span data-field="year">{{ year }}</span>, the maximum wages and self-employment income subject to social security tax increases to <span data-field="max_wage">{{ max_wage }}</span>.</p>
          <p>Modified AGI limit for traditional IRA contributions. Increased. For <span data-field="year">{{ year }}</span>, you may be able to take an IRA deduction if you were covered by a retirement plan at work and your modified AGI is:</p>
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item">Less than <span data-field="ira_limit_1">{{ ira_limit_1 }}</span> if married filing jointly or single (withover).</li>
            <li class="list-item">Less than <span data-field="ira_limit_2">{{ ira_limit_2 }}</span> if single or head of household.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>If you file a joint return and either you or your spouse was not covered by a retirement plan at work, you may be able to take an IRA deduction if your modified AGI is less than <span data-field="ira_limit_3">{{ ira_limit_3 }}</span>.</p>
          <p>Modified AGI limit for Roth IRA contributions. Increased. For <span data-field="year">{{ year }}</span>, you may be able to contribute to your Roth IRA if your modified AGI is:</p>
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item">Less than <span data-field="roth_limit_1">{{ roth_limit_1 }}</span> if married filing jointly or qualifying widow(er).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
