      <div>
        <div class="section-heading">Publication 517 (2012)</div>
        <div class="content-text">
          <p>For ministerial services you perform as a member of a religious order or sect, you may be exempt from SE tax. See Table 1.</p>
          <p>For members of a recognized religious sect, you may be exempt from SE tax. See Form <span data-field="form_number_18">{{ form_number_18 }}</span>.</p>
          <p>For more information, see the instructions for Form <span data-field="form_number_19">{{ form_number_19 }}</span>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-heading">Tax Forms and Instructions</div>
        <div class="content-text">
          <p>Schedule SE (Form 1040). Includes in gross income. To figure your net earnings from self-employment, use Schedule SE (Form 1040).</p>
          <p>Schedule SE (Form 1040). Includes in gross income. To figure your net earnings from self-employment, use Schedule SE (Form 1040).</p>
          <p>Table 3. Figuring Nonfarm Net Earnings</p>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th style="width: 30%;">Nonfarm income is:</th>
                <th style="width: 35%;">Two-thirds of your gross nonfarm income.</th>
                <th style="width: 35%;">Not applicable.</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>More than <span data-field="amount_1">{{ amount_1 }}</span> less</td>
                <td><span data-field="amount_2">{{ amount_2 }}</span>.</td>
                <td></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p>Actual net earnings. Mutual yearly total earings subject to SE tax by <span data-field="percentage_se">{{ percentage_se }}</span> (92.35) to get your net earnings from self-employment. See Schedule SE (Form 1040) instructions.</p>
          <p>Income Tax: Income and Expenses. Some income and expenses are treated the same for both income tax and SE tax purposes. See instructions for Schedule SE (Form 1040).</p>
          <p>Income Items. The tax treatment of offerings and fees, rentals, allowances, rental value of parsonage, and other items is discussed in the instructions for Schedule SE (Form 1040).</p>
          <p>Offerings and Fees. If you are a member of the clergy, you must include in your income offerings and fees you receive for religious services. See instructions for Schedule SE (Form 1040).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

